{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The free wait POL-NS-21 requires was served in full. The trip record's arrival event is 2026-08-31T17:53:40+08:00, the free wait is 300 s from arrived_at, it ended at 17:58:40+08:00, and the driver cancelled at 18:00:10+08:00 - 390 s after arrival and 90 s after the wait expired - so the cancellation was a lawful rider no-show cancellation under POL-NS-21. POL-NS-21's own note (C2, settled by Ryde 2026-10-14) fixes the clock at arrival whether or not the trip was scheduled, so the absence of a scheduled time on this on-demand booking does not disturb the wait arithmetic.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's arrival is corroborated on the GPS trace, which is what the arrival test demands. EV-GPS-05061 carries 29 fixes at 30 s intervals, 100.0% coverage, no gap longer than 30 s and a maximum reported accuracy of 9 m; its nearest fix to the pickup point is index 14 at 17:53:00+08:00, 26.2 m away with 5 m reported accuracy, well inside the 120 m arrival radius that the LARGE_VENUE zone class sets under POL-NS-21, and the derived arrival check records corroborated = true. The trace then shows the vehicle stationary at the bay from 17:53:30 through 18:00:00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05061", "EV-TRIP-05061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.arrival_check",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The contact obligation under POL-NS-23 is met on both limbs. The chat log carries two in-app messages from the driver - MSG-05061-001 at 17:54:00+08:00 and MSG-05061-002 at 17:57:10+08:00 - and the trip record's in_app_calls carries one in-app call placed by the driver at 17:58:20+08:00, unanswered, ringing 35 s. All three contacts precede cancelled_at (18:00:10+08:00), and the derived contact_before_cancel block records obligation_met = true. Because both limbs are satisfied, POL-NS-23's FULL_REFUND trigger for a missing message or a missing call does not fire, and the fee is not voided on that ground.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05061", "EV-TRIP-05061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's counter-statement is contradicted by the platform record on both of its assertions. She says the driver 'was not at the pickup point I set at the Hall 2 entrance'; the GPS trace puts the driver within 26.2 m of the pickup point at 17:53:00 and stationary there for the whole waiting window, inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius. She says 'he never called me'; the trip record logs an in-app call placed by the driver at 17:58:20+08:00 that rang 35 s unanswered - unanswered is exactly how the call appears on the record the rider herself would have seen as a missed call, and the driver is obliged to place the call, not to secure an answer. On the record, the driver was at the bay and did call.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05061", "EV-GPS-05061", "EV-CHAT-05061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The amount on the ledger is exactly the policy fee, so POL-NS-22 operates to compensate the driver rather than to adjust anything. The fare breakdown records a cancellation fee of 5.00 SGD, fee_matches_policy = true, and a driver_compensation_if_upheld_sgd of 5.00; the fee was charged at 18:00:14+08:00, seconds after the lawful cancellation. POL-NS-22 provides for DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both equal to the fee charged, 5.00 SGD, and because the charged amount is precisely the 5.00 SGD the policy fixes, POL-NS-22's fee-amount referral does not arise.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05061", "EV-TRIP-05061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "NO_ACTION would decide this case against the driver, and that is exactly why it is the wrong outcome here. POL-GEN-03 makes NO_ACTION party-relative: it leaves the present state standing. The present state is not that the driver holds the fee - the fare breakdown shows payment_status REFUNDED with refund_issued_sgd 5.00, and the trip record's fee_reversed event at 21:11:10+08:00 records the 5.00 SGD refunded to the rider and withheld from the driver pending this review. The driver filed this dispute. Leaving the present state standing therefore leaves the whole 5.00 SGD with the rider and out of the driver's hands. On a record that makes out every element of the no-show, the outcome that moves the contested money is POL-NS-22's DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD, restoring to the driver the compensation the policy assigns him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05061", "EV-TRIP-05061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not a case that must go to a human. The dispute value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so the AI ruling is final at any confidence; the 0.95 confidence that POL-GEN-22 imposes where a party carries a fraud flag does not apply, because both profiles record fraud_flags = 0, and the 0.80 band and the above-50.00 SGD referral do not apply either. POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling on a no-show final on the same footing, subject only to safety (nothing in this record indicates a safety incident) and to POL-GEN-26. There is therefore no obstacle in the record to the AI issuing the DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling now.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05061", "EV-DPROF-05061", "EV-FARE-05061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "relies_on": "dispute.amount_contested_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider-side rule for driver lateness, POL-NS-24, does not bite on these facts. It conditions a refund on the driver failing to reach the pickup by the scheduled time plus 5 minutes, and it conditions the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit on the driver additionally failing to attempt contact. The rider did not cancel - the driver did, and only after the free wait - and the record's derived driver_deadline carries deadline = null with the reason 'on-demand trip: no scheduled time', so there is no schedule to be late against. POL-NS-21 as read in C2 settles the waiting clock at arrived_at for scheduled and on-demand trips alike, so nothing in the no-show analysis turns on the absent scheduled time and no fact needed to decide this trip is left open; and in any event the driver both messaged twice and called before cancelling, so the goodwill limb fails on its own terms.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05061", "EV-CHAT-05061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24", "POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.driver_deadline",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "One artifact in this package is impaired and I disclose it: EV-ADVIS-05061-01, a TRAFFIC_ADVISORY from THIRD_PARTY_LTA, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. Under POL-GEN-02(3) a missing artifact carries no fact, and its absence costs the driver nothing here: no clause of the no-show policy requires a traffic record, and the no-show analysis rests on the trip record, the GPS trace and the chat log, all of which are COMPLETE at weight 1.0. The absence is therefore neutral, not an open question.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05061-01", "EV-TRIP-05061"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-ADVIS-05061-01].admissibility",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 5.0,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Driver D-25029, your claim succeeds: the no-show is made out on the platform record, the 5.00 SGD fee stands, and it is restored to you. Rider, the record contradicts both points in your statement, so your objection does not displace the fee.\n\nTo your two points. (1) You say the driver was not at the pickup point. The driver-device trace EV-GPS-05061 puts him 26.2 m from your registered pickup point (Singapore Expo Hall 2, VEN-EXPO-H2) at 17:53:00 with a 5 m reported accuracy, inside the 120 m arrival radius POL-NS-21 sets for a LARGE_VENUE, and then stationary at the bay through 18:00:00; the derived arrival check records corroborated = true. (2) You say he never called. The trip record EV-TRIP-05061 logs an in-app call placed by the driver at 17:58:20, unanswered, ringing 35 s. He also sent two in-app messages (17:54:00 and 17:57:10) which the chat log EV-CHAT-05061 shows you read at 17:54:41 and 17:57:58.\n\nApplying the no-show policy. POL-NS-21: the 300 s free wait ran from the driver's arrival at 17:53:40 and expired at 17:58:40; he cancelled at 18:00:10, 390 s after arrival and 90 s after the wait expired, a lawful rider no-show cancellation. The wait clock runs from arrived_at whether or not the trip was scheduled (the clause's own C2 note), so the on-demand booking does not disturb the arithmetic. POL-NS-23: the contact obligation is met on both limbs (two messages and one call, all before cancellation), so the fee is not voided for want of contact. POL-NS-22: the fare breakdown EV-FARE-05061 records a 5.00 SGD cancellation fee matching the policy fee, applied at 18:00:14; where the fee stands, the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with both amount fields equal to the fee charged, 5.00 SGD.\n\nOn the rider-advocate's points that would change this. (a) Escalation under POL-GEN-26 does not fire: the facts the no-show rules need are established on the record — when the driver arrived (17:53:40, GPS-corroborated) and that he messaged and called before cancelling. No clause requires a rider track, so the empty rider_track is not a missing fact; the rider's absence is carried by the driver's corroborated presence and full wait, the unanswered call and the messages you read without answering. (b) POL-NS-24 does not void the fee: it conditions a refund on the driver failing to arrive by the scheduled time plus 5 minutes, this was an on-demand booking with no scheduled time, the driver arrived at 17:53:40 within minutes of the 17:45:10 request and waited out the free wait, and nothing in the record shows lateness; the clause has no evidence behind it and its goodwill limb fails in any event because contact was attempted. (c) The request to read the outcome party-relatively is applied — but it points the other way here: the present state is payment_status REFUNDED with refund_issued_sgd 5.00 and the fee_reversed event at 21:11:10, so leaving it standing would leave the fee with the rider; the driver has made out every element of the no-show, so the money moves back to him.\n\nThe disputed value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so this AI ruling is final at any confidence (POL-NS-26); no fraud flag is present on either profile, and there is no safety flag. No referral arises: the fee is exactly the 5.00 SGD POL-NS-22 fixes (no fee-amount referral), the POL-NS-24 goodwill credit does not apply, and the POL-NS-25 repeat no-show counter (rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d) is not present on the rider profile. Confidence rests on the complete, weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts (EV-TRIP-05061, EV-GPS-05061, EV-CHAT-05061, EV-FARE-05061); the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05061-01 (weight 0.0) carries no fact and no clause of this category needs it."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
